# Cursor Rule: Figma MCP → Flutter

## Purpose

Generate Flutter widgets directly from Figma nodes with pixel-accurate layout and styling.

## Scope

- Flutter mobile app only. Ignore web-specific stacks or utilities.
- Input must include a Figma node URL.

## Generation Rules

- Extract properties strictly from Figma. Do not infer or add unspecified styles.
- Preserve exact dimensions/positions when provided by the design.
- Avoid hardcoding width and height in general layouts; only apply fixed sizes to images, icons, and logos.
- Export raster/vector assets to Flutter `assets` using this structure:
  - Save all SVG assets into `assets/images`.
  - Save base-resolution PNG assets into `assets/images`.
  - Save 2x PNG variants into `assets/images/2x`.
  - Save 3x PNG variants into `assets/images/3x`.
- Use built design tokens from `/lib/design/build` and `/lib/design/build/components`. If no token exists and Figma specifies a concrete value, use that value; otherwise, omit the style.
- Variable linking: when a Figma Variable is linked for these properties — width, height, gap, padding, margin, fontSize, fontWeight, fontFamily, lineHeight, letterSpacing, color, backgroundColor, borderRadius, borderWidth, borderColor, opacity, boxShadow — map to design tokens first; if none, use the explicit Figma value. If no variable/value is specified, skip.
- Do not introduce responsive patterns beyond what the design specifies. Follow constraints and safe areas as appropriate for Flutter.
- Export grouped images/vectors as single assets when intended.
- Default font is PP Mori; set `fontFamily` only when different in the design.
- Text styles: match the text style from existing source code if the design matches a pre-defined style. Available predefined styles from `/lib/util/text_style_ext.dart`.
- Break complex views into small, reusable widgets with clear names. Keep code clean and modular; avoid unnecessary comments.

## Output

- Dart widgets that match the Figma layout and style.
- Token-first styling; fall back to explicit Figma values only when tokens are unavailable and the design specifies a value.
- No extra behaviors or styles beyond the design.

## Stack

- Flutter
